From b6e7ee72b00bde05046db64f8727050e55df54c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:07:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P2-printing-module-application-contracts

Printing Module, Phase 2 (Application layer: contracts, DTOs, errors, localization,
options only - no implementations yet):

Contracts (ApplicationLayer/Contracts, not yet wired into IUnitOfWork - that lands
alongside their implementations, mirroring the R2/R3 split from the Branch Requests
module):
- IPrinterRepo, IMaticaPrinterConfigRepo, IRibbonTypeRepo,
  IMaticaProductPrintConfigRepo, IEvolisProductPrintConfigRepo, IPrintImageRepo
- IPrintImageStorage: pure I/O abstraction, no DB (mirrors IBatchFileEncryptor)
- IProductPrintConfigComposer: shared validation/staging core for product print
  configuration, extracted the same way ITransferComposer was - one implementation
  of the Matica/Evolis payload-matching, ribbon-type, and HEX-color rules, shared by
  product creation (single-aggregate design) and the standalone PUT sub-resource

Service contracts (ApplicationLayer/ServicesContracts, not yet wired into
IServiceManager - lands with their implementations):
- IPrinterConfigurationService: full CRUD, system-admin-only writes (Q-09)
- IProductPrintConfigurationService: GET/PUT sub-resource (Q-07), built on the composer
- IPrintImageService + UploadPrintImageRequest

DTOs: ApplicationLayer/DTOs/Printing/PrintingDtos.cs - printer CRUD DTOs, ribbon type
response, Matica/Evolis product print config request/response pairs, discriminated
ProductPrintConfigResponse wrapper, PrintImageUploadResult (with optional Warning
per Q-10's duplicate-name replace flow). Deliberately does not yet touch the existing
CreateProductRequest/UpdateProductRequest in ProductDtos.cs - that extension lands
with ProductService's orchestration of the composer.

Errors: ApplicationLayer/Errors/PrintingErrors.cs - 25 error codes across Printer /
ProductPrintConfig / PrintImage groups. Fixed a latent gap found in the existing
Product/Branch/Tenant AlreadyDeleted/NotDeleted errors while writing the Printer
equivalents: those omit .WithArg(), which silently drops the id from the Arabic
translation (falls back to untranslated English). Printer.AlreadyDeleted/NotDeleted
call .WithArg() correctly.

Options: ApplicationLayer/Options/PrintImageOptions.cs - RootPath, PublicBaseUrl,
MaxSizeBytes, AllowedExtensions.

Localization: Messages.resx / Messages.ar.resx (Egyptian colloquial) - all 25 error
codes, verified 1:1 key parity between EN/AR and between .WithArg() call sites and
{0} placeholders (no orphaned or missing placeholders in either file).

Flagged assumptions requiring confirmation before P3:
- Printer.UsingPrinterType treated as immutable after registration (hardware fact,
  not a business choice like Product.UsingPrinterType) - not explicitly locked
- Print-config sub-resource UPDATE (PUT) assumed to follow ProductService's existing
  non-admin-restricted authorization; Q-09 only locked the CREATE flow and the
  printer-registry writes as system-admin-only
